Subject: [PATCH 11148/11362] [outer-loop] Wire the foreign-checkout guard
 tree-wide (REQ-WORKTREE-IMPORT-1)

Third of the three triaged audit findings.

The guard refuses a run whose tests come from one checkout while import carnot
resolves to another, the trap that makes a worktree mutation proof read GREEN
while measuring the main checkout. It was wired into tests/python/conftest.py.
pytest loads a conftest only for its own directory and descendants,
tests/python is not an ancestor of tests/archive, and this repo has no root
conftest.

So the named missed input ran with the guard never loaded. Measured before:
collecting tests/archive/test_weight_steering.py reported 23 tests collected
and no check was performed. Verified after: the same collection refuses at
conftest load when PYTHONPATH points at another checkout.

Scoped to tests/ rather than the repo root deliberately. A root conftest would
load for every pytest invocation including ones that should not import carnot;
tests/ is the smallest directory covering the concept.

The incident test runs pytest in a subprocess, because the refusal happens at
conftest load and cannot be seen from inside a loaded session. Its fixture
copies the real guard module into the foreign tree: a stub carnot died on
ImportError instead, so the first version asserted the wrong failure and would
have passed with the guard removed. Recorded because that near-miss is the same
decorative-test class the mutation discipline exists to catch.

3 tests, 2/2 mutations RED including deleting the new conftest.

Also specs REQ-HARNESS-INTEGRITY-1 from the previous commit, which had none.

